# contracts-elide — the L1/L3 layering under elision (§Q4, FR-5): with
# `:elide`, the lowered contract guards (TrapIfFalse, trap 20) pass through,
# while the interpreter-enforced subtype ranges (L3, trap 21) still trip —
# guard elision flips L1 ONLY. Pinned at the transcript level (full traces).
:fuel 100000
subtype Percent = i64 range 0..100;
: no-sevens ( i64 -- i64 bool ) dup 7 == not ;
: add-safely ( i64 -- i64 ) needs [ no-sevens ] 1 + ;
:noelide
7 add-safely drop
150 as Percent drop
:elide
7 add-safely drop
150 as Percent drop
:stack
